      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/spring_creek_colony_montana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The colony sits at the western foot of the South Moccasin Mountains, 14 miles northwest of Lewistown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_Creek_Colony%2C_Montana",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Big Spring Creek, a perennial northwest-flowing tributary of the Judith River, supplies irrigation water for the colony's crops and livestock.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/spring_creek_colony_montana",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The community endured World War I persecution, leading to its closure in 1918 after 17 of 18 families fled to Canada.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/spring_creek_colony_montana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The colony's elevation is 3,514 feet, placing it in a semi‑arid continental climate with hot summers and cold, snowy winters.",
